  "notes": "USAGE:\n{張|は}り{合|あ}う implies a determined, sometimes stubborn competition. The competitor is marked with と or に. It often has a slightly negative nuance of pointless or stubborn rivalry.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {張|は}り{合|あ}う: to compete with\n- {張|は}り{合|あ}い: competition, rivalry (noun form)\n- {張|は}り{合|あ}いがある: to feel a sense of worthwhile competition\n- {張|は}り{合|あ}いがない: to feel there's no challenge\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{競|きそ}う focuses on straightforward competition. {張|は}り{合|あ}う adds a nuance of stubbornness or determination not to be outdone.",
